{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:4021-1","published":"2026-09-07T07:42:20Z","modified":"2026-09-13T18:23:16.109232489Z","related":["CVE-2024-25629","CVE-2025-31498","CVE-2025-62408","CVE-2026-33630","CVE-2026-69184","CVE-2026-69186"],"upstream":["CVE-2024-25629","CVE-2025-31498","CVE-2025-62408","CVE-2026-33630","CVE-2026-69184","CVE-2026-69186"],"summary":"Security update for c-ares","details":"This update for c-ares fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2024-25629: out of bounds read in ares__read_line() (bsc#1220279).\n- CVE-2025-31498: use-after-free in read_answers() when process_answer() may re-enqueue a query (bsc#1240955).\n- CVE-2025-62408: c-ares 1.32.3-1.34.5 use after free() (bsc#1254738).\n- CVE-2026-33630: Use-after-free / double-free in c-ares query-completion handling, remotely triggerable via\n  ares_getaddrinfo() over TCP (bsc#1270416).\n- CVE-2026-69184: CPU-exhaustion denial of service via unbounded DNS name compression pointer chains (bsc#1276290).\n- CVE-2026-69186: Memory-amplification denial of service via unvalidated DNS header record counts (bsc#1276291).\n\nChanges for c-ares:\n\n- updated to 1.36.8.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"c-ares","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Micro 5.3","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/c-ares&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Micro%205.3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.34.8-150000.3.29.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libcares2":"1.34.8-150000.3.29.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:4021-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"c-ares","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Micro 5.4","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/c-ares&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Micro%205.4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.34.8-150000.3.29.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libcares2":"1.34.8-150000.3.29.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU